try></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HASHIMOTO, HIDEYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OHYA, JUNICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAKAUE, SEIICHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A downflow liquid film condensation evaporator that is capable of reliably uniformly distributing and introducing evaporation fluid into evaporation passages and that is intended to simplify the construction thereof and reduce the manufacturing cost. The condensation evaporator comprises a liquid storing section (36) disposed above a heat exchanger core (34), and a liquid distributing means (37) disposed above evaporation passages (33) for uniformly distributing the evaporation liquid stored in the liquid storing section (36) to the evaporation passages (33).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un évaporateur de condensation de type film liquide à circulation descendante, capable de distribuer et d'introduire, de manière uniforme et fiable, un fluide d'évaporation dans des passages d'évaporation, et dont la fabrication est supposée être simplifiée, et les coûts réduits. L'évaporateur de condensation comprend une section de stockage (36) de liquide placée au-dessus d'un noyau d'échangeur de chaleur (34), et un organe de distribution (37) de liquide disposé au-dessus des passages d'évaporation (33), afin de distribuer uniformément le liquide d'évaporation stocké dans la section de stockage (36) aux passages d'évaporation (33).</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml un